  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMATRAN ORANGUTAN (PONGO ABELII) REINTRODUCTION, POPULATION RESEARCH AND ENHANCING COMMUNITY CONSERVATION STEWARDSHIP ACEH, INDONESIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS, BY THE END OF 2024, TO RELEASE AT LEAST 160 INDIVIDUAL ORANGUTANS IN JANTHO NATURE RESERVE (24 ORANGUTANS RELEASED DURING THE PROJECT PERIOD) AND TO PROTECT AND REDUCE ILLEGAL ACTIVITIES IN JANTHO NATURE RESERVE. PROJECT OBJECTIVES INCLUDE THE FOLLOWING: (1) REHABILITATED SUMATRAN ORANGUTANS ARE RELEASED AND MONITORED IN JANTHO NATURE RESERVE (2) JANTHO NATURE RESERVE (16,000 HA) IS PROTECTED BY THE ADDITION OF A SECOND PATROL TEAM, AND RANGER CAPACITIES ARE ENHANCED, BY ENSURING MONTHLY PATROL MISSIONS TAKE PLACE, COMMUNITY RANGER TRAINING TAKES PLACE, AT LEAST 2 EVENTS PER YEAR COVERING SUBJECTS INCLUDING REPTILE MAMMAL SURVEYING METHODS, SMART (SPATIAL MONITORING AND REPORTING TOOL) DATASHEET FORMATS, GPS TRAINING, SINGLE ROPE CLIMBING, AND FIRST AID AND (3) THE SIX PROJECT COMMUNITIES ARE INFORMED AND ENGAGED IN ACTIONS TO PROTECT LOCAL FOREST BIODIVERSITY, INCLUDING SUMATRAN ORANGUTANS.</narrative>
  </description>
